<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ernest I, Duke of Saxe-Altenburg</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1826">1826</a>–<a href="/years/1908">1908</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ernest I was Duke of Saxe-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/altenburg">Altenburg</a> from 1853 until his death in 1908. A Prussian general, he led his small Thuringian duchy into the North German Confederation in 1867 and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/german-empire">German Empire</a> in 1871, and fought in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/franco-prussian-war">Franco-Prussian War</a>. He was succeeded by his nephew Ernest II.</p></div>
